  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  name: orthonym\n  version: \"1.0.5\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/${{ name[0] }}/${{ name }}/${{ name }}-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 5a6a254fb0005a0bb2004eade1fda1de897a99daa5d7dfe3620e87ae5e28a65f\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script:\n    env:\n      # The OPSIN and centres jars are not part of this package. They are\n      # downloaded (with a SHA-256 check) the first time Orthonym needs them,\n      # or ahead of time with `orthonym --fetch-jars`.\n      ORTHONYM_SKIP_JAR_PREFETCH: \"1\"\n    content: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n  python:\n    entry_points:\n      - orthonym = orthonym.cli:main\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - hatchling\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - rdkit ==2026.03.5\n    - lxml ==6.1.3\n    - jpype1 ==1.7.1\n    - openjdk >=11\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - orthonym\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    script:\n      - orthonym --help\n\nabout:\n  summary: Rule-based IUPAC names from molecular structures (SMILES)\n  description: |\n    A SMILES string goes in. A verified IUPAC name comes out, or a clear \"no\".\n    Never a guess. Orthonym needs a Java runtime (installed with this package)\n    and the pinned OPSIN and centres jars, which it downloads with a SHA-256\n    check the first time it needs them (or run `orthonym --fetch-jars`).\n  license: MIT\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - NOTICE\n  homepage: https://github.com/Steinbeck-Lab/Orthonym\n  repository: https://github.com/Steinbeck-Lab/Orthonym\n  documentation: https://steinbeck-lab.github.io/Orthonym/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - Kohulan\n",
